    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "People can now be retired from a date, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass on the first run.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **Stored data:** a new migration, `V15__person_retired.sql`, adds a `retired_from` date to each person (empty means not retired). Each person sent to the screen now also carries `retired` and `retiredFrom`.\n- **Retiring:** a new endpoint, `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/{personId}/retire`, takes `{from}`. If the date is blank it uses the sheet's today. It saves the date, then writes `PERSON_RETIRED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=\u2026 from=\u2026` to the audit file. A bad date is refused with nothing written. Retiring doesn't change the person's version, and it writes no rollup line, since no total changes.\n- **Claim rule:** a claim dated after the person's retirement date is refused, with the reason shown in the claim form's error. This applies in three places: adding a claim from the row, the quick-add bar, and editing a claim. Claims dated on or before the retirement date are still allowed, including ones added later.\n- **Screen** (`People.tsx`):\n  - A \"show retired\" checkbox (`show-retired`), kept in the URL as `showRetired`. It's off when the screen first opens, and loading a sheet doesn't change it.\n  - Retired people's rows are hidden unless the checkbox is on. Their claims still count in the due total and the claimed total.\n  - Each row shows `person-retired` (yes/no) and `person-retired-from`, with a date field and a Retire button.\n  - Statement and retire share the row's single `person-error` element, and taking either action clears it.\n\n**Choices the request didn't settle**\n\n- Retiring someone already retired just moves their date; it isn't refused.\n- Claims already dated after the retirement date stay as they are. Retiring isn't refused because of them, and one of the test scenarios relies on this.\n- Editing a claim is only checked when its date actually changes. So an existing claim dated after retirement can still be edited if its date stays the same.",
